	"reviews": [
		{
			"updated_at": "2018-02-12",
			"author": "Toliman",
			"rating": 9,
			"provider_id": 1,
			"content": "I used to watch this quasi religiously, but Trevor Noah is the Anti-Stewart. \r\nPost-John Stewart, really needs a new category and deserves a 2/10 rating, it routinely hits the shallow end or just deceives people in an attempt at humor.\r\n\r\nI sometimes come across clips of Noah's standup or the monologues / interviews on Youtube, but it is shallow, and Trevor &amp; Team irritates and condescends. Have I changed so much in ~5 years, or has the show changed into a desperate and clinging example of failure. \r\n\r\nDisappointing."
		},
		{
			"updated_at": "2020-08-21",
			"author": "ChuckMCCluck",
			"rating": 1,
			"provider_id": 1,
			"content": "If your brain is empty enough to actually find Trump jokes for the millionth time funny then maybe you'll like this show. Don't know exactly what the hell will happen if Trump ends up losing this years election cause Noah will just be all out of material."
		},
		{
			"updated_at": "2020-08-29",
			"author": "ADL",
			"rating": 7,
			"provider_id": 1,
			"content": "I grew up with the Jon Stewart era, but I think it's recent years have been significantly less appealing. The writing has lost a lot of its cut given how American politics have developed over the past years, and Trevor Noah just doesn't really work for me."
		},
		{
			"updated_at": "2024-02-18",
			"author": "RickDB",
			"rating": 10,
			"provider_id": 1,
			"content": "Good to see old team back in full swing,\r\nThe new host line up needs some time to settle in and hope they can keep it going in this new format."
		},
		{
			"updated_at": "2024-10-08",
			"author": "Dr. Zo\u00efdberg",
			"rating": 8,
			"provider_id": 1,
			"content": "Monday nights\u2019.sharp tong of John Stewart is the best criticism of current events."
		},
